# SDLC Document Artifacts

When creating or editing these files, keep the required section headings. Do not invent alternate top-level schemas.

## `requirements.md`

- `# Requirements`
- `## User Story`
- `## Clarifications (Q&A summary)`
- `## Functional Requirements`
- `## Non-Functional Requirements`
- `## Acceptance Criteria`
- `## Out of Scope`
- `## Open Questions (if any remain)`

## `architecture.md`

- `# Architecture`
- `## Overview`
- `## Goals & Constraints (from requirements)`
- `## Component Diagram (mermaid)`
- `## Components & Responsibilities`
- `## Data Flow`
- `## Technology Choices (with rationale)` — default: **Python web application**
- `## Interfaces / Contracts`
- `## Security & Secret Handling`
- `## Failure Modes & Resilience`
- `## Open Trade-offs`

## `design-review.md`

- `# Design Review`
- `## Summary`
- `## Findings` (Critical / Warnings / Suggestions)
- `## Decisions Agreed`
- `## Architecture Updates Made`
- `## Residual Risks`
- `## Approval Status`

## `impl-plan.md`

- `# Implementation Plan`
- `## Approach Summary` — Python web app + Playwright verify path
- `## Task List (dependency order)` (table with ID, Task, Depends On, Priority, Status, Notes)
- `## Critical Path`
- `## Blocked Tasks`
- `## Test Strategy Preview` — unit/integration + Playwright MCP E2E
- `## Definition of Done (per task / overall)`

## Stage response files (`docs/sdlc/*-response.md`)

After every stage, write a response MD with:

- `# Stage <N> Response — <Stage Name>`
- `## Summary` — what was produced and why
- `## Artifacts` — paths created/updated
- `## Key Decisions`
- `## Open Questions / Blockers`
- `## PR` — PR URL or “pending” if creation failed
- `## Ready for Human Approval` — yes/no + what to confirm

Use the matching `sdlc-*` skill for full templates when writing a new file from scratch.
